#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162424 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162133 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e47d5ac-cb51-5259-ba41-6c407a992271" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation Using Column Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8e49ff5-5c55-5932-a2f1-7a848d8e5168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159747} {:answer/id #uuid "f50a19d2-7686-5036-9fda-2c7cfb65685d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159748} {:answer/id #uuid "11aa0a8f-db62-5600-b456-f28719a8db92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159749} {:answer/id #uuid "318e7f37-9785-50f9-904a-0982b300409b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159750} {:answer/id #uuid "39848f47-3856-51e7-a5dc-d7b5b7461834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11aa0a8f-db62-5600-b456-f28719a8db92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159749} :answer-field/id #uuid "1af22238-7121-5859-8bd5-bb780f5bcb32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159746}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "19ba5fbe-8893-5e75-ba57-95612db5ff60" :question/math-academy-id "q-146151" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nFind $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y).\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{2}{8}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1) \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+1\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507520 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162126 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "59bd2280-5028-5261-a9ed-61d01d80c29a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation Using Row Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51ff1faf-f72f-51b1-9a41-b232017d9e4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506866} {:answer/id #uuid "87fa4b33-432e-53e4-8ccc-c901d910fc2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506979} {:answer/id #uuid "8c525deb-1443-541c-a05e-859d3ee8d221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506990} {:answer/id #uuid "a91f79cf-d84a-5e27-a15d-1e049344b711" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507048} {:answer/id #uuid "d92d19f9-1c6e-581a-bc74-5f492ccfe305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d92d19f9-1c6e-581a-bc74-5f492ccfe305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507144} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee51a275-768a-5d1a-b7eb-4dea46354461" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e1cf5949-b307-55a6-98be-a625aa439d82" :question/math-academy-id "q-146218" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n\nFind $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=2]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x).\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{11}{20}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{9}{20}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{8}{11}$ | $\\frac{3}{11}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{5}{9}$ | $\\frac{4}{9}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=2] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{5}{9}+2\\cdot \\frac{4}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507487 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162126 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "59bd2280-5028-5261-a9ed-61d01d80c29a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation Using Row Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "088d49e0-c82e-5cd6-8f5f-e0b08d657dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506691} {:answer/id #uuid "25814cba-6385-5805-bdc3-6c1c56c5b6fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506760} {:answer/id #uuid "318b00f2-d9c3-5f71-bb72-7b8165255f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506795} {:answer/id #uuid "b6b9e806-8fc4-51d2-9d6d-828c8e700591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507081} {:answer/id #uuid "bbe69078-af55-52bd-8802-99309fc63ba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6b9e806-8fc4-51d2-9d6d-828c8e700591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507081} :answer-field/id #uuid "467dbca5-cb88-55f2-b3ea-8b97bc52fb4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507277}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc1054f2-f10b-59d2-b83a-b0b6686c6f7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-146241" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $0$ |\n\nFind $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=2]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x).\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{3}{5}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{5}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=2] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{5}{6}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}+\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507498 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162133 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e47d5ac-cb51-5259-ba41-6c407a992271" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation Using Column Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23541082-651d-51a2-9219-c871b4a40342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506752} {:answer/id #uuid "2d18daf1-a89c-5713-91c3-d8ce5523fce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506787} {:answer/id #uuid "86cecdff-ce99-5916-ac93-2adee2ea2db9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506975} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ab4007-433e-57e4-8aaa-5a872cc00e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507067} {:answer/id #uuid "b617e6f8-2d8e-5651-92d8-5fa6d7b738b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0ab4007-433e-57e4-8aaa-5a872cc00e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507067} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d21ab09-5097-55b4-ac6e-076877380491" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c6ab1dd3-6cd6-5880-b052-cdaa36ea1ea0" :question/math-academy-id "q-146279" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{20}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ |\n\nFind $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y).\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{20}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{3}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507517 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162133 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e47d5ac-cb51-5259-ba41-6c407a992271" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation Using Column Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4246cded-9692-5de5-855b-ca3b45401604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506832} {:answer/id #uuid "6ed7d84f-6aee-5298-8fbd-46a5560df2b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506934} {:answer/id #uuid "73d40450-3a18-5730-af9e-bc56d420e365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506945} {:answer/id #uuid "7ef16f12-6150-50a7-b5f6-6671c1cad720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506957} {:answer/id #uuid "848179a1-4988-551e-97b9-c41119f12cb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "848179a1-4988-551e-97b9-c41119f12cb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506972} :answer-field/id #uuid "9da998a7-6b78-5c75-b7e5-80e57209549b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ddd252ad-d6a4-5854-a4ad-0a75f711299e" :question/math-academy-id "q-146283" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |\n\nFind $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=3]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y).\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{7}{16}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{4}{7}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{3}{7}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=3] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+4\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
